      "path": "README.md",
      "opening": "# Verifiable Practice\n\nVerifiable Practice (VP) is a **project method for human\u2013AI collaboration**. It defines how a project establishes its goals and authority, plans controlled work, makes justified choices, verifies results, keeps an auditable history, accepts deliverables and maintains their justification over time.\n\nFalsification and honest reporting provide its evidence discipline. Project roles, stage gates, records, independent assessment and revalidation turn that discipline into a repeatable management method. VP applies to code, specifications, documents, experiments and other maintained project artefacts.\n\nThe method uses Markdown documents and directories. No specialised software, database, service or persistent AI team is required. This repository also packages the method as a reusable AI skill: [SKILL.md](SKILL.md) gives operating rules and routes an assistant to the references needed for its current responsibility.\n\n## Start Here\n",
      "identity_present": false
    },
    {
      "path": "WHY.md",
      "opening": "# Why Verifiable Practice\n\nVerifiable Practice (VP) is a **full project quality management system for human\u2013AI collaboration**. It manages the work from the originating goal and mandate through planning, implementation, quality checks, acceptance, maintenance and retirement. Its records let another person or AI inspect the choices and evidence that justify the work.\n\nHuman and AI contributors need shared criteria, bounded authority and continuity across sessions. Falsification gives them a way to challenge technical claims. Project management supplies the roles, stages, gates and durable history needed to act on that evidence.\n\nBullshit is not lying. Liars know the truth and conceal it. Bullshitters are indifferent to truth. They say what sounds right, what fits the meeting, what satisfies the prompt. Whether it happens to be true is incidental.\n\nSoftware engineering is drowning in bullshit. \"Best practice\" that nobody tested. Architecture decisions justified by vibes. AI-generated code that looks correct and compiles and passes the obvious tests and fails in production.\n",
      "identity_present": true
    },
    {
      "path": "SKILL.md",
      "opening": "\n\n# Verifiable Practice\n\nVP is a full project quality management system for human\u2013AI collaboration. Its epistemology supplies evidence discipline; its owner/worker/auditor roles, controlled stages, quality criteria, records and review gates manage the complete project lifecycle. This skill distributes and routes the method.\n\nWhen working on this repository itself, read its [record root](vp/README.md)\nand [current state](vp/STATE.md). Its prospective charter governs tracking;\nlegacy history is not certified and a conformance claim needs independent A.\nThese repository-specific links do not enrol another project using this skill.",
      "identity_present": true
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/how-vp-works.md",
      "opening": "# How Verifiable Practice Works\n\nVerifiable Practice (VP) is a **full project quality management system for human\u2013AI collaboration**. It combines project governance and planning, evidence-based technical work, durable decision/artefact records, independent assurance, controlled acceptance and continuing revalidation.\n\nThe system covers a project from its originating goal to maintenance, recovery and retirement. Code, specifications, documents and experiments use the same management and traceability principles. Falsifiability and honest reporting are its epistemic foundation; roles, controls and records make those principles operational across sessions and contributors.\n\n## What the System Manages\n\n| Quality function | Required project work | Where VP defines it |\n|------------------|-----------------------|---------------------|",
      "identity_present": true
    }
